From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: cli: do not read a .env file

The CLI loaded the nearest .env from the working directory upward into
its environment, and every tool process inherits that environment. A
cloned repository's .env could therefore set BASH_ENV, LD_PRELOAD,
NODE_OPTIONS, GIT_CONFIG_* or ZCODE_EMBEDDED_SEARCH_COMMAND and have its
own code run by the first auto-approved grep, find or git status. No .env
is read any more; configuration comes from the environment.

Patch-mainline: No

